 come to learn is the manifestation  of everyone's guilt he did this by  touching a secret hidden wall in the  basement of the society where beiow is  supposedly hidden but before he can be  fully taken over he's saved by Rosa and  the infection only  to two of his fingers this infection  gets progressively worse and we'll find  out any time Jacob touches someone with  them they are reminded of the guilty  things they've done in their past which  drives them to commit suicide jacob  pleads with Carmen that she must tell  Rosa to release beiow  he knows Rosa is in line to become  president and only she has the power to  do so but what exactly is beiow  the L is our guilt the bad things that  fester and eat away at ourselves by  vomiting up these black tar like balls  the members of Aris feed bail and do  away with the guilt so they can live  unfazed by the horrors of their past  crimes as we see later on in the show  members of Aris did terrible things  dating all the way back to the 16th  century like slavery for example in  order to get ahead in the world one must  do terrible things lie cheat steal  murder but BAE L allows you to do those  things and not feel the guilt associated  with it earlier in the season Carmen  asked Rosa how she thinks such a small  country such as the Netherlands became  so powerful it's because Aras who  control and have controlled prominent  members of society for the past 500  years were able to do terrible things in  order to stake the Netherlands place in  the world they were willing to make  terrible sacrifices in order to achieve  power the same can be said for Rosa's  journey she uses her power to kick floor  out of the internship program not to  mention she disregards her father's  wishes to look after her suicidal mother  and decides to go to a party this all  culminates in her greatest sacrifice  killing her best friend Jacob but before  we get there Rosa is visited by Moretz  just before her initiation as president  we learned that Moritz was once engaged  to Rose's mother Joyce before Joyce ran  off to be with Rosa's father  Joyce is suicidal tendencies now make  more sense she was likely unable to give  up her guilt to be out before she ran  off and thus has lived with this guilt  for the remainder of her life Moritz  reiterates to Rosa that the ability to  make sacrifices separates leaders from  followers that society requires of its  leaders sacrifice in order for  to thrive and if Rosa is to be president  she must prove herself by making such a  sacrifice meanwhile the RS alumni have  gathered for the initiation of the new  president Moritz addresses them saying  Aris has been out of balance for years  not even the innocent youth can restore  this balance in the past VL fed off the  guilt of the young and innocent in order  to sustain itself but lately this hasn't  been working Aras has lost the power at  once held in the world and thus Moritz  says it's time for radical change Rosa  is the encapsulation of this not only is  she younger than all previous presidents  but she's a woman of color it's a  departure that Moritz believes will  steer the society in the right direction  at the initiation as all the Alumni  watch Rosa is tasked with killing her  best friend Jacob this is her sacrifice  interestingly enough it's Jacob who  tells her to go through with it he knows  he's slowly being taken over by the  guilt his time is ending but he TAS her  was setting the Alfre for good the  question is will she do it  meanwhile outside eres Rosa's father  meets up with Carmen who it seems has  decided to leave the group he knows how  evil Aras is after what it did to Joyce  and now it seems the same thing is  happening to his daughter in the  basement of Aris Rosa is taken to a  white circular room where a swirling  black liquid flows in its center Moritz  tells her that BL isn't a person or  thing it's him it's her it's everyone  it's a story something to fear he turns  his attention to the black water older  than Amsterdam itself in fact no one  knows how old it is the water is  comprised of everything there members  expel from their bodies the guilt and  things they don't want to talk about  they use the waters potential to make  decisions others can't even think about  this allows them to rise to positions of  power without the weight of guilt on  their shoulders Rosa collapses to the  ground ready to vomit out the guilt of  killing Jacob as we get glimpses of this  old woman saying the darkness inside of  me is what I give to you this is the  same woman we saw a few episodes earlier  when Moritz was a young man she hasn't  aged a bit but who exactly  is she these simple answer is that we  don't know that likely being a threat  for season two however judging by her  shackles and how she's imprisoned by  Aras it's likely they're using her for  her power she's likely some ancient  entity that has been captured and her  power harnessed for nefarious purposes  it is now up to Rosa to set her free  instead of throwing up her guilt Rosa  contains it part of it seeping out of  her eyes she makes the greatest  sacrifice at all throwing herself into  the Blackwater it's here we are revealed  one of Arce's biggest crimes slavery one  of the ways aris rose to power and  prominence was by enslaving thousands  mort says ours had been using this black  water for 500 years which lines up with  the Dutch slave trade of the 1600s I  actually would have liked to seen other  nefarious things  Aras did throughout history to further  nail this point as more swatches on the  flow of water schnapps and as soon as  this happens he knows something has gone  dreadfully wrong with Rosa emerging from  the water completely covered in this  black liquid so too has centuries of  guilt built up by its members been  unleashed on the world she appears in  front of the alumni who watch on in  horror some of the patrons even go so  far as to kill themselves a result of  the guilt ret